# Chain-Retail WeChat Mall Mini Program · From-Scratch Rebuild Tutorial (CloudBase Edition)

> A tutorial-style skill: build a complete "chain stores + online mall" WeChat
> mini program full-stack system from zero. Contains NO real business data —
> export all data (products/stores/cards/secrets) from the original project
> or console at rebuild time.

## When to Use
- Building a chain-retail WeChat mall mini program from scratch (multi-store,
  pickup + delivery, membership & points)
- Cloning a similar project to a new AppID / cloud environment / merchant account
- Learning the full architecture of "mini program + CloudBase + H5 admin +
  in-store receipt printing"

## The System You Will Build
```
Customer (WeChat Mini Program) → Cloud Functions (30) → Cloud DB (21 collections) + Cloud Storage (images)
                               → WeChat Pay V3 / local courier API / subscribe messages / content safety
H5 brand site + admin (React+Vite static) → server PHP relay → cloud function gateway
In-store Windows receipt printer ← local print service (127.0.0.1:8899) ← H5 admin prints new orders on sight
```
Stack: native WeChat Mini Program (no Taro) + WeChat CloudBase
(cloud functions / cloud DB / cloud storage); no frontend build step.
H5 built with React 18 + Vite + Tailwind, deployed as static files.

## Step 1: Directory Skeleton
```
app.js/json/wxss          Globals: login, store geolocation, data loading, design tokens
pages/  31 pages = 5 Tabs (home/category/cart/membership/profile) + checkout flow
        + personal center + store-management consoles
components/  qty-modal (globally registered) + loading-lottie
utils/  data (product fallback) stores price cloud (DB wrapper) membership
        pinyin-search imgutil (image URLs) images avatars map-SDK libs/pinyin-pro
services/  cart (cross-store cart) coupons
cloudfunctions/  30 cloud functions (listed below)
h5-app/  React brand site + admin source (build artifacts go to the server)
print-server/  Node ESC/POS thermal receipt print service
```
app.json essentials: navigationStyle=custom (compute statusBarHeight yourself);
solid brand color for the nav bar; lazyCodeLoading=requiredComponents; declare
scope.userLocation and requiredPrivateInfos; packOptions.ignore to exclude docs
and keep the package small; pages not open to the public (e.g. invoices) can be
left unregistered in `pages` as hidden features.

