Key point: set the orders collection permission to "creator read/write only" →
staff order-taking MUST go through staffApi/orderApi cloud functions, never
direct frontend queries.

## Step 4: Core Business Rules (copy verbatim — one wrong change breaks everything)
1. **Three-branch pricing** (single source: utils/price.js): flash price inside
   its time window → use flash price, otherwise member price; strikethrough
   original price only when it exceeds the effective price; case-sale = spec
   pricing (packSpecs). Display / add-to-cart / order / checkout ALL go through
   the same function.
2. **Inventory semantics**: 0 = out of stock, >0 = in stock, no record = sold out.
   Deduction happens ONLY in the payment-success callback as a batch (reject the
   whole order if any item is short); case items deduct by bottle = qty × spec
   size; effective store = manual pick > geolocation > default first store.
3. **Cross-store cart**: every item binds a storeId; key = product + spec +
   store; filter/count/checkout by current store; legacy items (no store) belong
   to the default first store and do not drift; checkout settles one store at a
   time (grouped chained order creation); sync on store switch in onShow.
4. **Permission model**: super admin = all stores + staff management; card kinds /
   card lists / ads / coupons / points products / products / locations / web
   groups are super-only; store-bound admin = own store's orders/returns/
   inventory/close-store/gift cards/receipt printer; an admin with no store is
   treated as super; consoles always force the bound store. H5 login: super uses
   a dedicated account (phone left empty); admin/staff = phone + password.
5. **Points / membership**: designated premium categories matched by name keyword
   earn 1 point per ¥1, everything else 5 points per ¥1 (ratio configurable);
   3 tiers by cumulative points (basic / VIP / diamond); redemption via
   pointsApi; refunds claw points back.
6. **Refunds**: full refund including shipping before shipment; after shipment
   refund goods only, never shipping; refundStatus state machine keeps refunds
   idempotent.
7. **Reviews**: one review per order-item (deduped); text + image content-safety
   checks block only "risky"; displayed rating = (5 + average) / 2.
8. **Images**: convert every cloud fileID to a permanent direct link
   https://<appid>.tcb.qcloud.la/<path> (same conversion function on frontend
   and backend); Chinese characters / spaces MUST be URL-encoded — real devices
   load unencoded Chinese URLs unreliably; ≤20 main images and ≤20 detail images
   per product; keep existing images when an edit uploads none; 404 = re-upload;
   451 = CloudBase account frozen for non-payment (top up to restore — not a bug).
9. **Local courier**: base fare covers a base distance + per-km surcharge + cap;
   ALWAYS recompute server-side, never trust the frontend; courier returns are
   prepaid by the customer — never freight-collect.
10. **Public endpoints**: C-side reads for notices/activities/ads/rankings go
    through pub* actions (placed before auth checks); the frontend fetches on
    tab switch and falls back to static data on failure.
11. **Gift cards**: card-number search uses a server-side regex in the where
    clause (never filter only the current page); card secrets encrypted with a
    key from environment variables; state machine: inactive → activated →
    redeemed/frozen.
12. **Subscribe-message triggers**: order placed → staff new-order; status
    change → customer order status; refund → both sides.
13. **Pinyin search**: vendored pinyin-pro (no build); precompute _py (full
    pinyin) / _pys (initials) on products; element-level idempotency (check
    p._py — do NOT use a global _enhanced flag, async data replacement misses
    it); cloud cache + throttled refresh.

## Step 5: Pages (31)
- 5 Tabs: home (geolocation / banner ads / hot sellers / rankings entry / popup
  ad / fly-to-cart animation), category (two-level categories + search & filter
  + store switcher), cart (cross-store grouped selection / coupons / pickup
  modal), membership (tier card + points progress + coupon claiming), profile
  (role badges / system avatars / feature entries)
- Transaction flow: product detail (main-image carousel + separate detail
  images / multi-store stock / sold-out modal / review aggregation), checkout
  (grouped ordering / free-shipping threshold / coupons / courier fee),
  to-pay (wx.requestPayment / countdown), to-ship, to-receive, order detail
  (state machine / verification code / courier track map), order tracking,
  courier tracking
- Personal / marketing: address CRUD, coupons, points, points mall, favorites,
  browse history, profile edit, invite, activity page, store list, review-write,
  review-list, returns & exchanges (store / express / courier), rankings
- Management consoles: staff console (30s polling for new orders / status
  transitions / verification codes), store-admin console (orders / inventory /
  staff / close-store / returns tabs), return-audit, service-account binding
- Hidden: invoice apply / list (unregistered in app.json)

## Step 6: H5 Brand Site + Admin
React + Vite + Tailwind, single page with lazily loaded tabs: home / notices /
activities / stores (map) / admin / footer (ICP filing). The admin talks to the
cloud-function gateway via a dedicated PHP relay (the relay file lives only on
the server, not in the repo — keep it when deploying). Role control: super sees
global modules; store managers see only their store. The admin polls for new
orders → POST to the local print service.

## Step 7: In-Store Print Service
Local Node http service (port 8899): POST /print picks the printer by store
mapping → ESC/POS → auto receipt; GET /printers enumerates printers; GET/POST
/config manages the store→printer mapping; POST /test; GET /status. Ship with
auto-start + keep-alive scripts; stop the old service first to avoid port
conflicts; save .bat files containing Chinese in GBK; use the Unrestricted
execution policy for .ps1.

## Step 8: Deployment & Configuration
- Deploy cloud functions in dependency order: getOpenid → initDB → productApi →
  inventoryApi → adminApi → payApi/payNotify → orderApi/staffApi → pointsApi →
  reviewsApi → returnApi → serviceApi/sendSubscribeMsg → uuptApi/uuptCallback →
  invoiceApi → utility functions
- Env-var groups: payment quartet / courier quintet / service account / super
  credentials / card-secret key / admin passwords (copy values from the original
  environment or merchant platform — never write them into code or docs)
- WeChat Pay V3: merchant private key + serial number + APIv3 key; point the
  payment callback route at payNotify
- Subscribe-message template IDs live in sendSubscribeMsg
- Inject the map key into the H5 page
- H5 server: host the build artifacts statically + PHP relay; upload only the
  artifact directory, never bulk-overwrite the whole tree

## Pitfalls (hard-earned)
- Re-read .wxss from disk before editing + balance braces; record original
  values before tests mutate real data, restore afterwards
- Historical gaps in store ids are a migration artifact — do not re-sequence
- A React context missing a value prop → blank page (tsc passes, runtime
  crashes); after adding a field, grep the value block
- Cloud DB client limit is 100 → paginate with skip; _.in is limited to 20 →
  batch; when querying users by openid, stay compatible with _openid
- Product CSV import = match-and-update by id with NO delete semantics; the
  export file IS the import template
- Local printing / notification sounds use 127.0.0.1 — valid only on the
  store's own machine
- Put new adminApi actions inside the main try block, or they 404 after deploy

## Verification Checklist
- Compile in DevTools after every batch of changes; capture real-device
